  "id": "ema",
  "term": "EMA",
  "definition": "EMA, or ecological momentary assessment, is a clinical psychology method that repeatedly samples a person’s current behaviors and experiences in real time while they are in their everyday environment. It is used to reduce errors from later recall, capture more natural information, and examine short-term processes that affect behavior in real-world settings.",
